<article class="env-remark" id="070X">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/070X">Remark <span data-tag="070X">9.7.4.7</span>.</a> Let $\mathbb {K}$ be a collection of simplicial sets. Then the inclusion $\{  \Delta ^0 \}  \hookrightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt; \mathbb {K} }$ exhibits $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt; \mathbb {K} }$ as a $\mathbb {K}$-cocompletion of the contractible Kan complex $\{  \Delta ^0 \} $. In other words, for every $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the evaluation functor </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Fun}^{\mathbb {K}-\mathrm{cocont}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt; \mathbb {K} }, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\quad \quad F \mapsto F( \Delta ^0 ) \]
</div>
<p> is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories. This is a special case of Proposition <a data-tag="04BQ" href="/tag/04BQ">8.4.6.8</a>. </p>
</article>
